# Magical Hack's own example: "you may change 'swampwalk' to 'plainswalk'" (CR 612.2: the land type of a landwalk ability is a
# land type word). Bog Wraith has swampwalk: Bot2 controls a Swamp, so Bot2's Ornithopter can't block it (CR 702.14c),
# though it may block Bot1's other attacker. Magical Hack replaces Swamp with Plains in the Wraith's text (layer 3): it has
# plainswalk, Bot2 controls no Plains, and the Ornithopter blocks it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Bog Wraith
Ornithopter
Mox Sapphire
Magical Hack
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Ornithopter
Swamp x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bog Wraith.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Bog Wraith; Ornithopter > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Bog Wraith)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magical Hack.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Bog Wraith)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Swamp)
Bot1.Modes(Plains)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Bog Wraith.Keywords = Plainswalk
Bot1.Attack(Bog Wraith > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Bog Wraith)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Bog Wraith.Keywords = Plainswalk
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Life = 17
